"""Triton implementation of ``aten::_foreach_pow_.ScalarList`` (in-place).

``self[i] = pow(self[i], exponent[i])`` for every tensor of the list, mutating the
caller's tensors in place and returning ``None``.

Numerics follow ATen's ``pow_tensor_scalar``: every element is promoted to fp32
(opmath), the power is evaluated in fp32 and rounded exactly once when stored back
into the tensor's dtype.

Launch strategy:

* a uniform exponent (the common case) uses ONE fused kernel launch for the whole
  list; the per-tensor block ranges are recomputed inside the kernel from the
  runtime sizes so grid and kernel always agree;
* same-numel lists use a shorter launch signature (one shared numel);
* a heterogeneous exponent list falls back to one launch per tensor.

Because the exponent is uniform, it is classified on the host and specialized at
compile time (``MODE``/``FLAGS``): exponent 0.5 becomes a single vector sqrt and
the general path keeps ATen's 0/1/integral/odd/NaN cases as static branches.
"""

